# A modal sheet owns Enter even when the ask card's own BUTTON has focus.
#
# The sibling tests (an_overlay_{find,palette,search}_owns_the_card,
# an_overlay_owns_the_options_too) all focus an option ROW, which is inside
# ask_body_content -- so widgetOwnsEnter is false and Enter goes through
# drive_ask_keyboard, gated on keys_live(). This one focuses Approve and Deny,
# which live in ask_actions: widgetOwnsEnter is TRUE, the card's key handler
# steps aside, and the button's own activation is what Enter reaches. That
# path is gated on input_live() instead -- a different predicate, and the only
# test that covers it.
#
# What Enter does when it gets through is decide the approval: Deny resolves
# it, Approve resolves it, and either way drop_attach_ask retires the card and
# the command is gone. A modal sheet is on screen; the user is looking at
# settings, not at this. So the consequence to assert the absence of is the
# card's disappearance.
#
# `expect_no_text "Sending your answer..."` used to sit under both arms and
# was removed: busyId is set and cleared inside one loader tick against the
# in-memory mock, so that string is never on screen twenty frames later
# whatever Enter did. It could not fail, on any build, and it read like the
# assertion that was doing the work.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_ASK_DEMO=approval HANABI_TEST_OVERLAY=settings

require_thread t2
expect_text "The agent needs approval"
expect_text "./scripts/release_batch.sh --force"
# The sheet really is up -- otherwise the arms below would be testing an
# unobstructed card and passing for the wrong reason.
expect_text "Appearance, behavior, notifications, and local data"

# Deny is asked for focus and takes a real Enter. Two things stop it, and
# `focus_ui` failing to stick is the first: while the sheet is up the card's
# buttons are not focusable at all, so focus stays out on the sheet's own list.
# Enter therefore reaches no button, the approval is not decided, and the card
# is still on screen, undecided.
focus_ui ask_decline
key ENTER
wait_frames 20
expect_text "The agent needs approval"
expect_text "./scripts/release_batch.sh --force"

# Same for Approve.
focus_ui ask_submit
key ENTER
wait_frames 20
expect_text "The agent needs approval"
expect_text "./scripts/release_batch.sh --force"

key ESCAPE
wait_frames 20
expect_no_text "Appearance, behavior, notifications, and local data"

# Control arm. With the sheet gone the button takes the same key it just
# refused, and a successful resolve retires the ask -- so the card goes. If
# Enter never reaches the button (deleted, unbound, uninjected) the approval
# is still sitting here and this fails.
focus_ui ask_submit
expect_focused ask_submit
key ENTER
wait_frames 25
expect_no_text "accept — press Approve to try again."
expect_no_text "The agent needs approval"
